{"I built up an imposing position against Sax, but was then seized by maniac delusions that I was a reincarnation of Morphy. I was wrong." (Keene, BCM)} 1. e4 g6 2. d4 Bg7 3. Nc3 d6 4. Be2 Nf6 5. h4 h5 6. f3 Nc6 7. Be3 O-O 8. Qd2 (8. Nh3) 8... e5 9. d5 Nd4 10. Bxd4 exd4 11. Qxd4 c6 12. dxc6 bxc6 13. Qd2 Rb8 14. O-O-O Rxb2 $4 (14... Qa5 15. Bc4 d5) ({Now} 14... Be6 {is very strong - probably winning (Keene):} 15. b3 (15. Qxd6 Qa5) 15... Nd7 16. Bd3 Nc5) 15. Kxb2 Nxe4 16. fxe4 Qb6+ 17. Kc1 Qc5 18. Nb1 Be6 19. c3 Rb8 20. Nf3 Qa5 21. Qc2 Bxc3 22. Qxc3 Rxb1+ 23. Kd2 Rb2+ 24. Kd3 Qa6+ 25. Ke3 Rxe2+ 26. Kf4 Rxg2 27. Rhg1 Rf2 28. Rxd6 Qb6 29. Rxe6 {Sources: BCM, June 1972, p209; The Chess Player 1972/2; Dragon (Cambridge University CC bulletin), Easter Term 1972} 1-0

